; THE ROC — the size ladder's high end (GAMEPLAY-DESIGN V2, flown and approved
; 2026-08-10). A 3 m manned aircraft: *"once i lifted off, i feel the x10 momentum
; that this quad has."*
;
; `hull` is 100, the same as every other frame, because V.q4 is still open: are
; hull/armor physical quantities or abstract game currency? Until that is
; answered, holding them equal across the ladder keeps SIZE the only variable —
; which is the whole point of being able to fly all three in one map.
;
; `evasion_style` is stated because a roster's evasion identity should be readable
; in the roster's files — but it is NOT measured for this frame. The jink was
; measured best for the Kestrel and worst for the Atlas (v1.81); nobody has flown
; the reference pilot in a 500 kg airframe. Treat it as a default, not a finding.
;
; component_armor rotor 0.024 — PROVISIONAL, MEDIUM, and it is the human's own
; worked example rather than a derivation (Iteration 17 / E.q7): *"say the Roc is
; heavy AND powerful, so i would equip it with medium armor, because it may be
; more expensive so i would protect it more."* Armour follows from VALUE and
; EXPOSURE, never from a ratio against another frame.
;
; Half a raider bolt: a bolt strips 0.048 of rotor capability at the shipped
; severity, and 0.024 turns away half of it. MEDIUM is the whole of the design
; statement — it blunts the roster's standard small arm and defeats nothing. A
; value of 0.048 would make the Roc's rotors immune to raider fire outright, which
; is the invulnerability E6 forbids in spirit, and no frame gets it.
;
; It is the most-plated frame on both of E.q7's axes at once: 500 kg and 3 m of
; airframe to hang plate on, the roster's highest value to protect, and the
; roster's worst exposure — 52% of the rounds fired at it connect, against the
; Kestrel's 8.7% (E2, `swarm_bench` v2.46).
;
; THE MASS IS NOT PAID YET, and that is an honest gap rather than an oversight.
; E.q7's fiction is a loop — *"the engineer would have to reinforce it with armor,
; which would then make it heavier, affecting the balance"* — and today plating is
; free: nothing on this frame gained a gram for carrying it. Closing that loop
; means a mass cost, and mass is a flight-feel number and therefore the human's.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="FrameConfig" load_steps=3 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://resources/frame_config.gd" id="1_frame"]
[ext_resource type="Resource" path="res://resources/default_flight_roc.tres" id="2_flight"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_frame")
frame_id = &"roc"
display_name = "Roc"
flight_config = ExtResource("2_flight")
hull = 100.0
component_armor = {
&"rotor": 0.024
}
evasion_style = &"jink"
